---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import {
	APP_NAME,
	CONTACT_EMAIL,
	LEGAL_UPDATED,
	OPERATOR,
} from "../site.config";
---

<Layout title={`Privacy policy — ${APP_NAME}`} description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles your data.`}>
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pt-10 sm:px-6">
		<p class="label">Last updated {LEGAL_UPDATED}</p>
		<h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy policy</h1>
		<article class="prose-legal mt-6">
			<p>
				{APP_NAME} is a workout log operated by {OPERATOR} ("we", "us"). The short version: your workouts, body
				stats and settings are stored only on your phone. The only personal data that reaches our servers is what
				you need to sign in.
			</p>

			<h2>What stays on your phone</h2>
			<p>These are saved in a database on your device and are never sent to us:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Your profile: name, age, gender, height, body weight, training split, experience level and goal.</li>
				<li>Every workout: exercises, sets, weights, reps, times, notes and personal records.</li>
				<li>Routines, custom exercises, units, rest-timer and reminder settings.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Workout reminders and rest-timer alerts are local notifications scheduled by your phone. We don't collect a
				push token or any device identifier.
			</p>
			<p>
				When you choose <strong>Export backup</strong> or <strong>Export spreadsheet</strong>, the file is handed to
				your phone's share sheet. Where it goes from there (Drive, email, a chat) is up to you and governed by that
				service's policy.
			</p>

			<h2>What we store on our servers</h2>
			<p>
				Sign-in is handled by Supabase, our authentication provider. When you sign in with Google or Apple, we
				receive and store:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Your email address (Apple may give us a private relay address instead).</li>
				<li>Your name and profile picture URL, if your Google or Apple account shares them.</li>
				<li>A user ID from the sign-in provider, and when your account was created and last signed in.</li>
				<li>
					Technical logs the authentication service keeps for security, such as IP address and device user agent
					at sign-in.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>We use this only to let you sign in and keep your account secure.</p>

			<h2>What we don't do</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>No advertising, and no ad or tracking SDKs in the app.</li>
				<li>No analytics on how you use the app.</li>
				<li>We never sell or rent personal data, and we don't share it except with the processors listed below.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Service providers</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Supabase</strong> — hosts our sign-in service and account database.</li>
				<li><strong>Google</strong> — if you choose "Continue with Google", to verify your identity.</li>
				<li><strong>Apple</strong> — if you choose "Continue with Apple", to verify your identity.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
			<p>
				Your account data is kept until you delete your account. Data on your phone stays until you erase it in
				Settings, delete your account, or uninstall the app.
			</p>

			<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
			<p>
				In the app, go to <strong>Settings → Delete account</strong>. This removes your account from our servers
				immediately and erases all data on the phone. You can also ask us by email — see{" "}
				<a href="/delete-account">Delete your account</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				You can ask for a copy of the account data we hold, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to{" "}
				<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we'll reply within 30 days. Your workout data is
				already in your hands: export it from Settings at any time.
			</p>

			<h2>Health information</h2>
			<p>
				{APP_NAME} is a training log, not a medical device. Body stats you enter are used on your phone to show
				units and starting weights and are not shared with us.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>{APP_NAME} is not meant for children under 13, and we don't knowingly create accounts for them.</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>
				If we change this policy — for example when push notifications or cloud backup are added — we'll update the
				date at the top and tell you in the app before the change applies to you.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				{OPERATOR} · <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
			</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>
